#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
msgid "What are derived accessions:"
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
msgid ""
"In some cases, you may want to add new accession names that have special "
"relationships to other stock types in the database. For example, after "
"preliminary phenotypic screening of progenies derived from different crosses "
"in a trial, you may want to add new accession names for some plants in that "
"trial."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
msgid "Allowed Stock Types:"
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
msgid ""
"The derived accession (stored as accession stock type) can be linked to "
"another accession, or plant or tissue sample in the database."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{bold}Derived from accession{end_bold}: e.g., new accession derived from "
"another accession because of a mutation."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{bold}Derived from plant{end_bold}: e.g., new accessions derived from plants "
"originated from crosses or family names in trials."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{bold}Derived from tissue sample: {end_bold} e.g., new accessions derived "
"from tissue samples via tissue culture."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
msgid "Linkage between derived accession, direct source and original source:"
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
msgid ""
"Relationship between each derived accession and its source is displayed on "
"the accession detail page and its source detail page (accession/plant/tissue "
"sample)"
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{bold}Additional Info Section:{end_bold} Both direct source of that derived "
"accession and its origin are displayed in the Additional Info section. If "
"the direct source is a plant or tissue sample, the original source will also "
"be provided (e.g., if the direct source is a plant in a trial, the original "
"source of that plant name can be accession, cross or family name)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{bold}Pedigree:{end_bold} Pedigree information of each derived accession "
"depends on stock type of the original source (accession or cross or family "
"name)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/breeders_toolbox/derived_accession_usage_info_dialog.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{bold}Originated from a cross or a family name:{end_bold} The female parent, "
"male parent and cross type of the cross or family name are used as parents "
"and cross type of the derived accession. If the derived accession is "
"originated from a cross, the accession is also stored as a progeny of that "
