#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
msgid "About Plant Cell Walls"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Plant cell walls are typically considered as complex structural matrices "
"that surround all plant cells."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"They consist mostly of polysaccharides, but also contain components such as "
"lignin, structural lipids and proteins in specialized cell types."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Plant {link}cell wall{end_link} model"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"However, the term \"plant cell wall\" is also used more broadly to refer to "
"the entire compartment outside the plasma membrane that forms a continuum "
"throughout the plant, also termed the \"apoplast\", or apoplastic "
"compartment."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Green fluorescent protein that has diffused throughout the cell wall and "
"apoplastic compartment surrounding an onion epidermal cell."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cell_wall.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Scale bar represents 50 micrometers."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas mason/secretom/index.mas
msgid "The Tomato Fruit Cuticular Cell Wall Proteome"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The plant cuticle is a highly specialized hydrophobic cell wall that covers "
"the aerial organs of land plants and provides protection against "
"desiccation, pathogens, UV radiation and herbivory."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"It is continuous with the outer-periclinal polysaccharide cell wall of the "
"epidermis and consists of organic soluble waxes embedded in, and layered on, "
"a non-soluble polyester matrix of ω-substituted fatty acids."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The waxes include both aliphatic compounds, derived from very long chain "
"fatty acids, and secondary metabolites, such as triterpenoids and flavonoids."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Little is yet known about many key mechanisms of cuticle biogenesis, and "
"experimental strategies to identify new proteins that associate with cutin "
"and waxes could provide a valuable means to identify new candidates."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Although Arabidopsis research has greatly accelerated the discovery of new "
"cuticle-related genes, its cuticle poses some experimental limitations since "
"it is relatively thin, fragile and difficult to isolate in substantial "
"quantities."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Conversely, tomato fruit cuticles are astomatous and large amounts of intact "
"cuticular material can be isolated for chemical and biomechanical analyses."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"For example, the fruit accumulate on the order of 1 mg cm{sup}-2{end_sup} "
"cutin, compared to the stem of Arabidopsis, which has 0.5-10 μg "
"cm{sup}-2{end_sup}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Thus, the typical 6 week period of early tomato fruit development represents "
"a remarkably rapid and extensive phase of cuticle biosynthesis."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Light microscope image of the surface of an expanding tomato fruit with the "
"cuticle stained red."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"To identify new candidate proteins with a potential role in cuticle "
"biosynthesis, and particularly those that are secreted to the apoplast, we "
"are generating a more comprehensive inventory of proteins that are "
"associated with the outermost surface tissues of plant organs, we are using "
"a range of complementary protein fractionation strategies (1D gel-based and "
"liquid chromatography) coupled with several sensitive mass spectrometry (MS) "
"platforms."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are also characterizing a number of tomato fruit cuticle mutants and have "
"developing a new 3D imaging technique using confocal scanning laser "
"microscopy for visualizing the architecture, deposition patterns and micro-"
"structure of plant cuticles."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This has allowed 3-D cuticle modeling based on the reconstruction of serial "
"optical sections and its use in the identification of several previously "
"unreported features of the tomato fruit cuticle."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This information, together with the proteome study is providing new insights "
"into the molecular processes underlying cuticle formation and restructuring."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/cuticle.mas
msgid "A 3-D rendering of the tomato fruit (cv. M8) cuticle."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
msgid "Functional Screens to Identify Secreted Proteins"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have been developing and applying functional screens to identify genes "
"encoding secreted proteins."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The genes are identified based on the ultimate localization of the encoded "
"protein, utilizing protein markers whose activities confirm targeting to the "
"cell surface."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
msgid "Sucrose plate with no yeast colonies growing (negative control)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The YST screen can be used to test a specific cDNA of interest, or to screen "
"a cDNA library."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The screen uses invertase, an enzyme that hydrolyzes sucrose to generate "
"glucose and fructose, as a reporter gene/protein and yeast ({species}) as a "
"host."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"If yeast cells are streaked onto plates containing sucrose as the sole "
"carbon source, they must secrete invertase to break down the sucrose in "
"order to grow, and so an invertase-deficient yeast mutant will be unable to "
"grow."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
msgid ""
"Sucrose plate showing yeast colonies transformed with the YST vector library."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This system can also identify plasma membrane (PM)-spanning or PM-anchored "
"proteins if the orientation of the fusion protein is such that the invertase "
"component is external to the cell."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The resulting yeast transformants can then be isolated and the plasmids "
"containing the heterologous transgenes sequenced, allowing identification of "
"the secreted protein."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We typically also confirm the localization of candidates of interest by "
"transient expression as GFP fusion proteins in onion epidermal cells, "
"coupled with staining using the FM-64 dye to co-stain for the plasma "
"membrane,"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
msgid "Yeast Secretion Trap (YST) Screen"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"A {species} leaf showing regions of HR indicating the presence of a secreted "
"protein fused to NIP."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have also developed a new technique termed the NIP secretion trap screen."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Briefly, this involves ligating cDNAs in frame at the 5’ end of the DNA "
"sequence encoding a gene termed necrosis-inducing protein (NIP) that has "
"been truncated to remove the native secretory signal peptide."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"NIP was identified from the oomycete {species}, as a protein that induces a "
"hypersensitive response (HR), resulting in cell death, in leaves of some "
"plants when present in the apoplast."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "It does not cause HR when expressed in the plant cytosol."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Constructs containing individual cDNA::Nip fusions are transformed into "
"{species}, which is then infiltrated into the apoplastic compartment of "
"{species2} leaves."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Any proteins encoding SPs will be secreted from infected plant cells as NIP "
"fusion proteins, causing a readily detectable HR."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Nip fusion assay is a convenient and rapid means to confirm secretion of "
"proteins in planta and complements the YST screen."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
msgid "Necrosis Inducing Protein (NIP) Secretion Trap Screen"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"A cytoplasmic protein (green) and a secreted protein (red) in plasmolyzed "
"onion cells."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Scale bar represents 50 microns."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Screen a range of tomato tissues for genes encoding secreted proteins, "
"focusing particularly on fruit development and leaves at various stages of "
"infections with {species}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Annotate the corresponding genes and confirm their localization in the cell "
"wall by transient expression as fluorescent fusion proteins in onion "
"epidermal cells."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Further examine the localization and trafficking pathways of candidates that "
"show unexpected localization in the apoplast."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"To date we have identified both known cell wall localized proteins as well "
"as a number of proteins whose presence in the apoplast is unexpected, based "
"on functional annotation, or the absence of a predicted secretory signal "
"peptide, suggesting alternative non-canonical secretion pathways, as have "
"describe in yeast and mammalian cells."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have also identified several proteins that show dual localization in the "
"wall an intracellular compartments, and we are now characterizing some of "
"the complexity in the secretory pathway."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/functional_screens.mas
#: mason/secretom/section_templates/objectives.mas
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas mason/secretom/index.mas
msgid "The Tomato Fruit Glycoproteome"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"SDS PAGE gel image showing tomato fruit proteins isolated by lectin "
"affinity, stained with Coomassie Blue (black) or glycoprotein stain (pink)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"As with all eukaryotes, N-glycosylation in plant cells is a common post-"
"translational modification for proteins traveling through the secretory "
"pathway, many of which are destined for the cell wall."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The large-scale isolation and analysis of glycoproteins by lectin affinity "
"chromatography, coupled with mass spectrometry (MS), has become a powerful "
"tool to evaluate the glycoproteome of mammalian cells; however, is has "
"rarely been used with plants glycoproteins."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are using affinity selection of glycoproteins using the lectin "
"Concanavalin A, coupled with two-dimensional liquid chromatography (2-D LC) "
"and matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry (2DLC-"
"MALDI MS/MS) and electrospray ionization MS (ESI-MS) analysis, to identify "
"extracellular and secretory pathway proteins, focusing on those expressed in "
"ripe tomato fruit."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Tomato has long served as model system for fleshy fruit development and "
"ripening is an excellent system to study cell wall proteins as it is "
"associated with dramatic changes in wall biology, including dramatic enzyme-"
"mediated cell wall polysaccharide degradation, apoplastic sugar metabolism "
"and extracellular defenses against microbial pathogens."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"In spite of this, there are few published proteomic analyses of ripening "
"tomato fruit and most of those are based on extraction of total proteins "
"followed by 2-DE separation, since the wall proteome was not the major "
"target."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Consequently, the protein extraction step was not optimized for secreted "
"proteins."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Computational prediction of the subcellular location of the N-glycoproteins "
"isolated from green mature tomato fruit with Concanavalin A."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This enrichment strategy has been highly effective, with a high proportion "
"the identified proteins showing predicted localization either in the "
"secretory pathway."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/glycoproteome.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are currently investigating the targeting of proteins from the secretory "
"pathway to other intracellular organelles."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
msgid "The Secretome of Phytophthora / Tomato Interactions"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Infection of tomato leaves (upper panels) by {species}, showing the early "
"asymptomatic biotrophic phase (left) and the later necrotrophic phase."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The {species} developmental stages (trypan blue staining) are shown in the "
"lower panel."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Plant pathogens can be classified into three groups, based on their "
"mechanism of infection: biotrophs, necrotrophs or hemibiotrophs."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Biotrophic pathogens penetrate the plant wall, parasitize host cells while "
"evading or suppressing defense responses and require viable host tissue for "
"pathogen nutrition and reproduction."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"In contrast, necrotrophs, overwhelm plants by secreting mixtures of "
"degradative enzymes that allow the pathogens to subsist on necrotized host "
"tissue."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Hemibiotrophic pathogens, such as the bacterium {species}, the fungus "
"{species2} and the oomycete {species3}, employ elements of both these "
"strategies in a biphasic \"stealth\" infection mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This involves an initial biotrophic phase, when the pathogen proliferates "
"asymptomatically in the host and efficient mechanisms must be employed to "
"evade and suppress host defenses."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Subsequently, in the second stage, hemibiotrophs orchestrate a physiological "
"switch from asymptomatic infection to large-scale necrosis and tissue "
"dissolution, presumably resulting from the coordinated secretion of factors "
"such as lytic enzymes and necrosis elicitors."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are using a range of strategies to characterize the secretomes of the "
"host and pathogen during the various stages of hemibiotrophy, including "
"{link} Yeast Secretion Trap Screen{end_link}, {link2} comparative proteomic "
"analysis{end_link2} of extracted protein populations, and deepsequencing of "
"the transcriptomes of the infected tissues using RNAseq."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"These samples correspond to a time course experiment of a compatible "
"interaction between {species} (clonal lineage US11) and its host tomato "
"(M82)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Tissue was collected at three different stages of the interaction and a mock "
"inoculated plant served as control."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/phytophthora_interaction.mas
#: mason/secretom/section_templates/data_items.mas
msgid "Data Sets"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
msgid "[Download]"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
msgid "Computational prediction of secreted proteins"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"A number of {link}computational tools{end_link} have been developed to "
"predict the presence of SPs."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"These programs have been greatly refined in recent years and their accuracy "
"has improved with the adoption of machine learning algorithms."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"However, while this is a valuable approach, as with all prediction-based "
"tools, there is a consistent error rate and both false positive and negative "
"predictions should be expected."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"One of our major goals is to identify the incorrect predictions and generate "
"a database of computationally and functionally confirmed secreted plant "
"proteins."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"It has been reported that one of the most effective predictors of SPs is "
"{link}SignalP 3.0{end_link}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have used both SignalP and our recently developed predictor, {link}"
"SecreTary{end_link}, to screen the predicted proteomes of several plant "
"species to date."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "See below for these prediction results."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have developed a new predictor, {link}SecreTary{end_link}, for more "
"accurate computational prediction of plant proteins that traffic through the "
"classical secretory pathway. {link}Try SecreTary{end_link},"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
msgid "New predictor: Secretary"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This will provide you with a list of predicted proteins, grouped by species, "
"with the annotation protein length, molecular weight, confidence scores for "
"the presence of a secretory signal peptide and predicted localization."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
msgid "Search SecreTary, SignalP, TargetP results for secreted proteins"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
msgid "SecreTary, SignalP, TargetP results"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/prediction.mas
msgid ""
"Other computational tools for prediction of ER-targeting signal peptides"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas mason/secretom/index.mas
msgid "Tomato Comparative and Quantitative Proteomics"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Tomato has long served as model system for fleshy fruit development, and is "
"an excellent system to study cell wall proteins as it is associated with "
"dramatic changes in wall biology, including enzyme-mediated cell wall "
"polysaccharide degradation, apoplastic sugar metabolism and extracellular "
"defenses against microbial pathogens."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"However, there are few published proteomic analyses of ripening tomato fruit "
"and most of those are based on extraction of total proteins followed by 2-DE "
"separation, and the wall proteome was not the major target."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Tomato leaves infected by {species}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Similarly, defense responses against pathogens are also fundamentally "
"associated with changes in the expression of secreted apoplastic proteins, "
"but there have been few systematic studies at the proteome level."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have been developing methods to obtain sample materials highly enriched "
"in apoplast/cell wall proteins, including vacuum dehydration, centrifugal "
"dehydration and several methods that involve the centrifugal isolation of "
"the cell wall followed by sequential extraction with solutions of increasing "
"ionic strength."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Taken together, the goal is to create a more comprehensive catalog of the "
"tomato cell wall proteome, focusing on fruit and leaves at various stages of "
"infection by the oomycete {species}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This will include both protein identification and quantitative data, to gain "
"insights into the dynamic properties of the tomato secretome."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Additionally we have been profiling \"total proteomes\"; and screening the "
"resulting protein populations for those known to be localized in the cell "
"wall with a predicted secretory signal peptide, or that are {link}"
"glycosylated{end_link}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have been applying several approaches for comparative proteomic analysis, "
"including Difference Gel Electrophoresis (DIGE), isobaric Tag Relative "
"Absolute Protein Quantitation (iTRAQ), exponentially modified protein "
"abundance index (emPAI) and MSE."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The latter two approaches were found to provide accurate relative "
"quantitation data on par with that provided by iTRAQ at significantly "
"reduced cost, but without the ability to multiplex."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"They have been integrated into our work flow and are used where appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have also developed a high/low pH reverse phase-reverse phase (RP-RP) "
"separation protocol to fractionate peptides prior to MS analysis."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This new approach complements the traditional strong cation exchange (SCX) "
"RP strategy and the Offgel peptide IEF fractionation."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Comparative proteomic analysis of the tomato-{species} pathosystem"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "DIGE gel of proteins from {species} infected tomato leaves."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are characterizing the dynamics of host-pathogen secretomes in leaves "
"during infection by the oomycete {species}, during distinct phases of "
"hemibiotrophic infection, using both DIGE and iTRAQ supported with 454-"
"generated transcript profiling."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
msgid "Comparative proteomic analysis of tomato fruit ripening"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Wild type ripe tomato fruit (left), and equivalent stage fruit from the nor "
"(middle) and rin (right) mutants."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/proteomics.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"While the genes responsible for all these mutations have been cloned, and "
"important progress has been made in elucidating their respective signaling "
"pathways, numerous aspects remain poorly understood and the degree of "
"regulatory complexity and the multiplicity of underlying molecular "
"mechanisms have far exceeded expectations."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
msgid "About Secretory Pathways"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The primary route for protein secretion from eukaryotic cells is termed the "
"classical, or endoplasmic reticulum (ER)/Golgi-dependent, secretory pathway."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Briefly, secreted eukaryotic proteins utilize an N-terminal signal peptide "
"(SP) to direct their co-translation on ER-bound ribosomes into the ER lumen, "
"after which they progress through the endomembrane system and are ultimately "
"exported to the extracellular environment, or cell surface."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"It should be noted that these represent a subset of SP-containing proteins, "
"since others are retained in the ER or Golgi or are redirected to other "
"compartments, such as the vacuole."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Schematic diagram of the plant classical secretory pathway, highlighting "
"protein co-translational translocation from ER-bound ribosomes in the ER "
"lumen and the subsequent major trafficking pathways (N, nucleus; ER, "
"endoplasmic reticulum, Chl, chloroplast; TGN, trans-Golgi network; PVC pre-"
"vacuolar compartment; PM, plasma membrane; CW, cell wall)."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"There is also growing evidence that plant proteins can be secreted to the "
"apoplast via routes that are independent of the ER-Golgi pathway."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Such proteins do not have canonical signal peptides and treatment with "
"chemical inhibitors, such as brefeldin A, which disrupt vesicle trafficking "
"between the ER and Golgi, and does not perturb secretion."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"While such non-classical pathways have been studied in {link}yeast{end_link} "
"and {link2}mammalian cells{end_link2}, and a {link3} search tool{end_link3} "
"is available for such mammalian proteins, essentially nothing is yet known "
"about such pathways in plants."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/secretion_path.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "This will be addressed in this project."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas mason/secretom/index.mas
msgid "Spin-off Projects and Collaborations"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Interspecific Reproductive Barriers in Tomato {link}{acronym}{end_link}"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This is an NSF Plant Genome program funded collaborative scientific endeavor "
"to identify and understand the biological processes underlying species "
"isolation within the Tomato family."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are using proteomic tools to study the molecular barriers between tomato "
"species, with particular focus on secreted proteins as these are believed to "
"be critical in establishing such barriers."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"We have been characterizing the proteomes of pollen, styles and pollinated "
"styles from both {species1}, {species2} and {species3}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
msgid ""
"The Evolutionary Origins of the Plant Cell Wall and Associated Secretome"
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Cells of {species}, a member of the Charophycean green alga, following "
"treatment with a microtubule inhibitor."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Pectin components of the wall are shown in green."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid "Microscopic imaging and cover design by {name}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"One of the most important phases of plant evolution occurred approximately "
"460-480 million years ago when photosynthetic organisms developed the "
"capacity to colonize land."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"This transition to harsh terrestrial conditions would have required the "
"ability to resist new abiotic stresses, including desiccation and UV "
"radiation, as well as the development of mechanisms to promote progeny "
"dispersal."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"It is likely that polysaccharide and cuticular cell walls were essential for "
"the transition to a terrestrial environment and yet the evolutionary origins "
"of their biosynthesis are not well understood."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/detail/spinoffs.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"Characterization of the secretomes of divergent members of the CGA will "
"likely provide insights into the mechanisms that are currently used by "
"embryophytes for primary, secondary and cuticular cell wall formation and "
"restructuring."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/index.mas
msgid ""
"A project to catalog and study the dynamic properties of the cell wall "
"proteome (the secretome), using tomato as a model system."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/index.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"The {link}plant cell wall/apoplast{end_link} plays a fundamental role in "
"many aspects of growth, development, and responses to environmental "
"conditions and assault by pathogens and insects. It is therefore not "
"surprising that a substantial portion of the plant proteome is localized in "
"the cell wall/apoplast. However, while major initiatives are now underway to "
"map the proteomes of many plant organelles, such as the {link2} "
"chloroplast{end_link2}, the cell wall proteome, or \"secretome\", is far "
"less well characterized than those of other subcellular compartments."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/index.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{strong}What is the \"secretome\"?{end_strong} The term \"secretome\" is "
"generally used to refer to the population of proteins that are secreted "
"outside the plasma membrane of a cell, but can also be used to describe the "
"subset of the proteome that enter the {link}secretory pathway{end_link}."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/index.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{strong}The purpose of this NSF-funded project{end_strong} is to catalog and "
"study the dynamic properties of the cell wall proteome, or secretome, using "
"tomato ({species}) as a model system."
msgstr ""

#: mason/secretom/index.mas
#, perl-brace-format
msgid ""
"{strong}Why study the \"secretome\"?{end_strong} Proteomic analysis of "
"cellular compartments reveals the subcellular locations of a specific "
"protein, or protein complex, which in turn can be a valuable step towards "
"understanding protein function. Localization information also helps in the "
"identification of protein interactions and targeting pathways, and peptide "
"motifs and structural signatures that can direct proteins to various "
"cellular locations. In addition the analysis of a subcellular proteome has "
"the advantage of requiring \"biological pre-fractionation,\" which can "
"substantially enhance the detection of lower-abundance proteins."
msgstr ""

